ps5webkit: decrypt RAR4 archives (RAR 3.x AES-128: data, and headers with -hp)

On top of 0001 (archive_rar_crypto.c: AES, and RAR 3.x's key derivation
with its SHA-1 quirk). The RAR reader's reads all go through rar4_ahead()
and rar4_consume(): after a main header with MHD_PASSWORD each header is a
salt and the header padded to 16 bytes, decrypted whole (the passphrase is
the one whose header CRC holds); a file's data (FHD_PASSWORD, version 2.9
and later) is one AES-128-CBC stream across its volumes, read through a
plain text view. RAR 3.x has no password check value: the data's key comes
from the passphrase that opened the headers, else the first one given, and
a wrong one shows as "Incorrect passphrase, or the archive is damaged
(...)". Stored files stop at their size (not the padding); an encrypted
link's target is read with the key, or left empty without one; RAR 1.5 and
2.x encryption stays unsupported.

The format follows UnRAR's behaviour; no UnRAR code is used.

diff -ruN a/libarchive/archive_read_support_format_rar.c b/libarchive/archive_read_support_format_rar.c
